===persian===

از کنار ..دشت
از جوار کوه....
از زلال آبی قدیم پرشکوه....
من به شهر دود آمدم....
من به شهر پر صدای بی سرود...
نه... به شهر بی امید خسته خمود آمدم..... عمر می گذشت....
آه می وزید...
مار خستگی... دست چیدن مرا....
چشم دیدن مرا...
پای رفتن مرا به راه عشق می گزید...
در چنین چم کبود... در چنین غروب غم....
در چنین خمار خسته خمود...
وای اگر خیال تو نبود
برق چشمه زلال تو نبود.
وای اگر صدای تو نبود... راز تو نبود
زخمه های ساز تو نبود
بازوان باز تو نبود
در شبان پر هراس شهر ...
مرد خسته ای در آرزوی ماه بود
زیر پای سایه های غم کوچه تو غرق آه بود...
در غروب این ستاره ها....
در صدای زخمدار این مناره ها...

در صدای دور
در صدای حجم های آهنین بی سرود.....
عمرها تباه بود.
شهر پرده ای سیاه بود
عشق روی تو چراغ راه بود.... شعله ای برای محو هر گناه بود...

۱۳۴۷

===machine===

From the side of the plain
From the side of the mountain...
From the clear blue of the old, glorious...
I came to the city of smoke...
I came to the city full of noise without a song...
No... I came to the city without hope, tired and hunched..... Life was passing by...
It was sighing...
The snake of fatigue... my hand-wringing...
My eyes seeing...
It was biting my feet on the path of love...
In such a blue sky... in such a sunset of sadness...
In such a drunkenness, tired and hunched...
Wow, if it weren't for your imagination
There wouldn't be the electricity of your clear spring.
Wow, if it weren't for your voice... There wouldn't be your secret
There wouldn't be your wounds
There wouldn't be your open arms
In the frightened shepherd of the city...
A tired man was longing for the moon
Under the shadows of sadness, your alley was drowning in sighs...
In the sunset of these stars...
In the wounded voice of these minarets...
In the distant sound
In the sound of songless iron volumes.....
Life was ruined.
The city was a black curtain
Love on you was a beacon.... It was a flame to erase every sin...

1347

===lantern===

From beside the plain,
from the flank of the mountain,
from the clear, old, glorious blue,
I came to the city of smoke...
I came to the city loud and songless...
no — to the hopeless city, weary and slumped... Life slid by...
a sigh kept blowing...
the snake of exhaustion bit my plucking hand,
bit my seeing eye,
bit the foot I set on the road of love...
In such a livid dusk... such a sorrowing sunset...
such a weary, slumped half-stupor —
oh, were it not for the thought of you,
the gleam of your clear spring;
oh, were it not for your voice... your secret,
the struck strings of your music,
your open arms —
through the city's terror-filled nights
a tired man went longing for the moon,
and under the shadows of grief your alley drowned in sighs...
In the setting of these stars,
in the wounded cry of these minarets,
in the far-off sound,
in the sound of songless iron hulks —
lifetimes lay ruined.
The city was a black curtain;
the love of your face was the lamp of the road,
a flame to burn away every sin.

1347

